course: dictionary
lesson: 1929
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Comic can be a thing you read, a word that describes something funny, or a person who tells jokes. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: «Sam, of all people, lends him his best comic.» You can lend a thing, and this comic is something you can read, so it means a book with pictures and speech bubbles. Check it by swapping in another meaning: «lends him his best funny» does not make sense.
explain: Comic can also be a describing word. «A comic moment» means a moment that makes people laugh. Ask yourself: is the word naming a thing, or describing one? A thing is a noun, and a describing word is an adjective.
fact: A comic is a book or magazine that tells a story with pictures in boxes and words in speech bubbles.
fact: Comic means funny, making people laugh, as in «a comic moment».
fact: A comic can also be a person who tells jokes.
fact: «Comics and graphic novels are real reading: you work out the story from the words and the pictures together.»
fact: A storyboard is «a plan made of pictures in boxes, like a comic», and film makers use storyboards to plan their films.
exercise: «Sam, of all people, lends him his best comic.» What is a comic here? | A kind of cake | *A book with pictures in boxes | A person who tells jokes | A funny moment
exercise: «The dog falling into the pond was a comic moment.» What does comic mean in this sentence? | *Funny, making people laugh | Wet and cold | Made of paper | Very sad
exercise: A girl reads a comic inside her blanket den. Which word is the best meaning of comic here? | *A book with pictures in boxes and speech bubbles | Funny, making people laugh | A plan for a film | A person who tells jokes
test: Tom's grandad is a comic on the stage, and he tells jokes all night. What is a comic here? | *A person who tells jokes | A funny moment | A book with speech bubbles | A storyboard
test: «A storyboard is a plan made of pictures in boxes, like a comic.» Which word in this sentence means a book with pictures and words? | pictures | *comic | storyboard | plan
exam: Maya says comic can be a book, a describing word, or a person. Which sentence uses comic as a describing word? | «She bought a comic at the library.» | *«The clown's tumbles were comic, and the crowd roared.» | «The comic told jokes all night.» | «A comic has speech bubbles.»
